---
/**
 * What the privacy notice says about counting visitors: the truth for the
 * site as it is built. Switched on in src/data/site.mjs, it describes the
 * counter. Switched off, it says there is none.
 */
import { counting } from '../data/site.mjs';
---

{counting ? (
  <Fragment>
    <p>
      This site counts page views with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, a
      small open-source counter, so that we can see which pages are read and which other sites send
      visitors here. It is the only part of this site that contacts anyone but the site's own host.
    </p>
    <p>For each page view it records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the page that was opened, and the page that linked to it, if any</li>
      <li>the name of the browser and the operating system, and the size of the screen</li>
      <li>the country the visit appears to come from</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It sets no cookie and stores nothing in your browser. Your IP address is not stored: it is
      used for a moment, in memory, to tell one visit from another and to work out the country, and
      is then discarded. The counts cannot be traced back to a person, and they are not combined
      with anything else we hold.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest is knowing, in numbers only,
      whether this site is found and read.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
) : (
  <p>
    This site does not count its visitors. It uses no analytics or tracking tools and no
    advertising services.
  </p>
)}
